Acts,root,Activities
6,Acts,6. IMPULSE PROCEDURE
6A,6,6A. MOVEMENT SEGMENT
6A1,6A,6A1: INVOLUNTARY MOVEMENT STAGE
6A2,6A,6A2: VOLUNTARY MOVEMENT STAGE
6A2.02,6A2,Determine which units will move his impulse (C1.4).
6A2.04,6A2,Move those playing pieces scheduled to move in accordance with the rules. See (C1.31). This will include base rotations on certain impulses (C3.7). This may include, on impulse #32 only, landing on or taking off from a planet (P2.41) or atmospheric flight (P2.8). Determine, but do not resolve, any damaged caused by movement.
6A3,6A,6A3: DAMAGE DURING MOVEMENT STAGE
,,In each of the following steps, allocate the damage (D4.0) as it is resolved, step by step.
6A3.06,6A3,Controlled mines can be ordered to detonate (M5.201). Resolve damage from mines (M0.0).
6A4,6A,6A4: FINAL MOVEMENT ACTIONS STAGE
6A4.01,6A4,Release ships from tractor beams (G7.0) if these systems were destroyed or lost power in this segment. (Involuntary release from stasis is in 6B6.)
6A4.02,6A4,Announce movement changes: intention to adopt/drop pursuit (C1.322), evasion (C1.3223), or station keeping plotting (C1.3224): drop/adept erratic maneuvers (C10.0): make speed changes under (C12.0); forgo or resume web passage status (G10.533). These decisions are made secretly and simultaneously in advance of all announcements in this step.
6A4.03,6A4,Reveal the presence of a minefield (M7.1).
6A4.04,6A4,Emergency deceleration takes effect (C8.0).
6B,6,6B. IMPULSE ACTIVITY SEGMENT
6B01,6B,6B1: INITIAL STAGE
6B01.02,6B1,Switch fire control from active (D6.6) to passive mode (Dl 9.0) or vice versa. This is the time for voluntary changes; involuntary changes [e.g. wild weasel (J3.0), cloak (G13.0)j occur as required at other points (D6.63).
6B02,6B,6B02: CLOAKING DEVICE STAGE
6B02.01,6B02,Activate (G13.14) or deactivate (G13.15) cloaking device.
6B02.02,6B02,Announce range and bearing if using hidden movement of cloaked ships (G13.61) on impulses #8 and #24.
6B02.03,6B02,Attempt to destroy own cloaking device (G13.162). This can only be attempted once in any period of 32 impulses.
6B03,6B,6B03: LOCKON STAGE
6B03.01,6B03,Roll to determine if lockon has been lost, retained, or regained due to changing conditions (D6.1). Note that this may be repeated several times during the impulse if conditions (particularly cloaked ships and WW) change. This is also the point at which self-controlled ATG and warp-seeking drones which are beyond tracking range of their targets lose tracking, and the point at which the conditions of (F3.31) are judged.
6B03.02,6B03,Scouts and carriers use reserve power to increase EW available for lending (H7.2). Legendary Weapons Officer uses his reserve EW point (G22.71).
6B03.03,6B03,Scouts begin or voluntarily end lending (G24.212). Scouts deploy reserve EW (G24.2114).
6B03.04,6B03,Tactical Intelligence Interrogations (D17.23) are conducted. Reports from probe drones (FD6.32) and (FD6.33) are received.
6B03.05,6B03,ECM drones begin to generate EW (FD9.12). Fighters change which EW source they are accepting lending from (J4.922).
6B03.06,6B03,Determine disengagement by separation (C7.21).
6B04,6B,6B04: SHIP SYSTEM FUNCTIONS STAGE
6B04.01,6B04,Detect individual mines (M7.2). Automatic mine detection (M7.34).
6B04.02,6B04,Reinforce web; recalculate strength (G10.3).
6B04.03,6B04,Web Step: Lay web (G10.23). Lay web anchors (G26.3). Assume or drop web anchor status(G10.116).
6B04.03a,6B04,SubSpace Fields are activated (OG14.23) or deactivated (OG14.242).
6B04.03b,6B04,Launch Mass Driver Missiles
6B04.04,6B04,Operate Tractors: Activate or release tractor beams (G7.0). This is the only time for voluntary activation or release; involuntary release may occur at various points (destruction of tractor, launch of WW, etc.). This could result in an immediate tractor auction (G7.414).
6B04.05,6B04,Attach pods to a tug (G14.4). (Pods are dropped in 6B10.)
6B04.06,6B04,Labs (G4.2), scouts (G24.25), Aegis (Dl 3.3), and SWACS (J9.12) attempt to identify seeking weapons and mines (M7.5).
6B05,6B,6B05: SCOUT FUNCTIONS STAGE
6B05.01,6B05,SWACS (J9.12) and scouts attempt to attract drones (G24.23), break lock-on's (G24.22).
6B05.02,6B05,SWACS (J9.2) and scout PFs (K1.756) go wild.
6B06,6B,6B06: SEEKING WEAPONS STAGE
6B06.01,6B06,SW Control Step: Voluntary transfers (F3.5) or release (F3.4) of control of seeking weapons. Involuntary transfers and releases can occur at many other points in the sequence (F3.53).
6B06.02,6B06,Drop electronic warfare pods (J4.9622).
6B06.03,6B06,Launch plasma torpedoes (FPl.3) and/or pseudo-plasma torpedoes (FP6.12).
6B06.04,6B06,MW Release Step: Deploy drones from MW drones (FD8.22) and SP shuttles (FD7.33).
6B06.05,6B06,Launch drones (FD1.2).
6B06.06,6B06,Launch probes (for info, not as weapon) (G5.2).
6B06.07,6B06,Drop chaff (D11.3).
6B06.08,6B06,ESG Step: De-activate and (subsequently) activate expanding sphere generators (G23.3) based on previous announcements. Announce operation of ESGs (G23.3); cancel previous announcement (G23.33). Size and strength are announced (G23.46).
6B06.09,6B06,SFG Step: Activate and (subsequently) de-activate stasis field generators (G16.11). Involuntary deactivations become effective (G16.14).
6B07,6B,6B07: MARINES ACTIVITY STAGE
6B07.01,6B07,Mutiny Step: First die roll for mutiny (G6.20).
6B07.02,6B07,Operate Shields Step: Drop shields; restore shields dropped previously (D3.5).
6B07.03,6B07,Operate transporters (G8.0), including the laying of T-bombs (M3.22). Block boarding by (G8.23). Resolve hit and run raids (D7.8) conducted by Transporter.
6B07.06,6B07,Mines laid two impulses previously by transporter become active 
6B08,6B,6B08: SHUTTLE & PF FUNCTIONS STAGE
6B08.01,6B08,Challenge enemy shuttles to a dogfight (J7.0).
6B08.02,6B08,Fighters may drop warp booster packs (J5.41).
6B08.03,6B08,Recover (land) shuttlecraft (J1.6), fighters, fast patrol ships (K2.31), web anchors (G26.35), and cloaked decoys (G27.3). Shuttles land on enemy ships (J1.65) and (J1.63).
6B08.05,6B08,Launch shuttlecraft (J1.5), fighters, fast patrol ships (K2.32), wild weasels (J3.0), suicide shuttles, scatter packs (FD7.0), and cloaked decoys (G27.3). Involuntary release of tractor beams to allow wild weasel launch (J3.452) may be a part of this action.
6B08.06,6B08,Move shuttles between shuttle bay and balcony (J1.53).
6B09,6B,6B09: SATELLITE SHIP FUNCTIONS STAGE
6B09.01,6B09,Recover satellite ships and energy modules (G19.412) via Transporter. (No recovery by DisDev.)
6B09.02,6B09,Launch satellite ships and energy modules (G19.411) via Transporter. (Launch by DisDev is in 6D5.)
6B10,6B,6B10: SEPARATIONS STAGE
6B10.01,6B10,Drop pods from a tug (G14.3).
6B10.02,6B10,Rear hulls of ships that separated 64 impulses previously are stabilized (G12.54).
6B10.03,6B10,Lay mines (other than by transporters) (M2.1) (M9.21). Mines laid in previous impulses become active if the conditions of (M2.34) are satisfied.
6B11,6B,6B11: FINAL FUNCTIONS STAGE
6B11.02,6B11,Active/deactivation Flame Shields (OG1.12) and Flame Shield Projectors (OG7.12)
6B11.03,6B11,Announce emergency deceleration (C8.0).
6B11.04,6B11,Activate Plasma Cloud Generators (OG3.12), Activate Sub Space Coagulators and announce formation (OG4.12)
6B11.05,6B11,Roll to determine new facing of tumbling ships (C6.5511). If this is the last tumbling impulse, see (C6.554).
6B11.06,6B11,Roll to reprogram the computer; impulses 8 and 24 only; see (G11.341).
6C,6,6C. DOGFIGHT RESOLUTION INTERFACE
6C02,6C,Fighters carrying booster packs may drop them (J7.72). Resolve any resulting separations. See also (J7.13).
6C03,6C,Announce intent to separate by breakaway (J7.711) and resolve any resulting separations.
6C05,6C,Launch dogfight drones (J7.53) within dogfight (by one shuttle in a dogfight against another shuttle in that same dogfight only).
6C06,6C,Drop chaff (D11.3) and (J7.55).
6C07,6C,Fire weapons at drones launched above if allowed by firing arcs (J7.56).
6C09,6C,Determine if dogfight drones (J7.53) or drones coming from outside (J7.32) of the dogfight hit their targets (or just what they did hit), and resolve damage.
6D,6,6D. DIRECT-FIRE WEAPONS SEGMENT
6D1,6D,6D1: FIRE ALLOCATION STAGE
6D1.01,6D1,DisDev Declaration Step: Announce intention to use displacement device on the current impulse, the unit to be displaced, and (if Andromedan) the direction in which displacement will be made (G16.31).
6D1.02,6D1,Fire Decision Step: All players secretly and simultaneously decide what direct-fire weapons to fire and the targets of those weapons. At this point, EW points being generated can be adjusted under (D6.315) by reserve power or various other means. (Note that lending of EW is adjusted in 6B3.) PPD wavelock release (E11.333).
6D2,6D,6D2: DIRECT-FIRE WEAPONS FIRE STAGE
6D2.03,6D2,First Hellbore Firing Option (E10.44). § Shield damage is marked, internal damage is recorded to be resolved in 6D4.
6D2.04,6D2,Direct-Fire Step: All Direct-Fire Weapons not listed separately fire. § Shield damage is marked; internal damage is recorded to be resolved later (E1.11) in 6D4.
6D2.05,6D2,Aegis Fire Steps: Weapons able to use Aegis Fire Control fire their remaining pulses (D13.0). ? Shield damage is marked: internal damage is recorded to be resolved in 6D4.
6D2.05.01,6D2.05,Aegis Fire Opportunity #2
6D2.05.02,6D2.05,Aegis Fire Opportunity #3
6D2.05.03,6D2.05,Aegis Fire Opportunity #4
6D2.06,6D2,Second Hellbore Firing Option (E10.44). § Shield damage is marked; internal damage recorded and resolved in 6D4.
6D5,6D,6D5: DIRECT-FIRE WEAPONS CONSEQUENCES STAGE
6D5.03,6D5,Displacement devices operate (G18.3) and can be used to launch satellite ships (G19.42).
6D5.06,6D5,Release ships from tractor beams (G7.0) if these systems were destroyed in this segment (Involuntary release from stasis is in 6B6.)
6D5.07,6D5,Electronic warfare (D6.3) benefits of any systems destroyed in Segment 6D are lost (e.g. scout channels destroyed, etc.)
6E,6,6E. POSTCOMBAT SEGMENT
6E1,6E,Roll for the possibility of UIM breakdown (D6.52).
6E2,6E,Start/stop erratic maneuvers takes effect (C10.0).
